  "id": "Compound::DB00511 - Gene::482",
  "verbalization": "Acetyldigitoxin appears to interact with Atp1b2 through a shared pathway involving Fxyd2 and potassium-transporting ATPase activity. The evidence suggests that Acetyldigitoxin binds to Fxyd2, which then participates in potassium-transporting ATPase activity, ultimately leading to Atp1b2 being involved in this process. This indicates a potential mechanism where Acetyldigitoxin may influence Atp1b2 through a common intermediate, Fxyd2, by modulating potassium transport. The overlapping roles of Fxyd2 in both sodium-potassium and potassium-transporting ATPase activities suggest a possible functional overlap, which could explain the co-participation of Atp1b2 in these processes. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible regulatory relationship between Acetyldigitoxin and Atp1b2, mediated through Fxyd2, which may be a key node in the molecular network governing ion transport and cellular homeostasis.",
